That fell right on his face.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.090
You could easily fracture your orbit

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.550
which is the bone surrounding your eye.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.440
Like imagine if it hit
him dead on into the eye,

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.830
you could lose the eye completely.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.050
But, what I don't understand
here is how it hit him

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.040
so perfectly on the forehead,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.590
but then didn't break his nose.

00:03:13.585 --> 00:03:15.291
(suspenseful music)

00:03:15.291 --> 00:03:19.456
(skin singing)
(Harry screaming)

00:03:19.456 --> 00:03:22.042
(Harry blowing)
(Harry screaming)

00:03:22.042 --> 00:03:23.316
(body thudding)
- Ow!

00:03:23.316 --> 00:03:24.812
(Harry yelling)

00:03:24.812 --> 00:03:25.645
(skin hissing)

00:03:25.645 --> 00:03:27.390
- Immediately after getting a burn

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.340
you don't wanna necessarily go and put it

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.710
into something icy because

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.300
that can actually exacerbate the burn

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.410
and make it feel worse.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.570
So, you wanna run your burn

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.410
under room temperature if anything.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.560
The danger of receiving a burn,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.670
especially on the hand, is when burns heal

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.390
they often form scar tissue
that form contractures

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.620
which actually lead the hand
to be in a flexed position.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.950
And when it's in a
flexed position like this

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.220
it makes it very difficult
for it to be usable.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.420
So, a lot of occupational therapy,

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.870
physical therapy, needs to be done

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.130
in order to return the hand to normal.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.790
Also important to remember
that there's multiple types

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.630
of burns from heat, meaning thermal burns,

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:08.760
electric burns, chemical
burns, there's even ice burns.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.090
Like if you hold dry ice onto your hand,

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:14.140
that's like minus 100 degrees
Fahrenheit or whatever it is,

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.130
you can burn your hand with the ice.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:18.110
That's why when we
recommend icing your knee

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.310
or your shoulder or something,

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.400
we always say put it
over a piece of fabric

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.860
so it's not directly on your skin

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.820
'cause then you can actually
cause yourself frostbite.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.420
Frostbite is essentially a burn.

00:04:27.273 --> 00:04:30.530
(feet squishing)

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:31.363
Oh no!

00:04:32.985 --> 00:04:36.251
(Marv yelling)

00:04:36.251 --> 00:04:37.084
(body thudding)

00:04:37.084 --> 00:04:39.570
Not only did he have a puncture wound

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.180
from a nail in his foot,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.440
he fell from like the eighth step.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.780
If you ever are to get
like a nail in your foot,

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.290
while it's important to get
it out after a period of time,

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.890
you don't wanna rush to do it yourself

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.290
in case that it's hitting an artery

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.370
and actually putting
pressure on that artery

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.750
and preventing you from bleeding out.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.600
'Cause it's very possible,
okay, you pull it out

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.710
and now you just have a
ton of blood coming out.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.240
And if you're not in a medical
setting to address that

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.678
that is a problem and make sure
your tetanus is up to date.

00:05:05.678 --> 00:05:06.905
(blowtorch blazing)
(Harry yelling)

00:05:06.905 --> 00:05:08.330
Oh!

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.163
No!

00:05:10.096 --> 00:05:10.929
Move!

00:05:10.929 --> 00:05:12.760
Oh, that's a full thickness
third degree burn.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.310
The way that we do it
in the medical setting

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.420
to decide how severe someone's burns are,

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.230
outside of the first,
second, and third degree,

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:21.680
we also give a percentage of
the total body surface area

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:22.513
that has been burned.

00:05:22.513 --> 00:05:23.760
And we use the rule of nines

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.660
and we decide what percentage is burned,

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.710
how we should adjust,

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.940
and we think about fluid replacement.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.530
If a large percentage

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.640
of the body surface area has been burned,

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.840
that cripples a person's
ability to keep their fluids.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.960
And they actually become dehydrated

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.450
and need fluids with
electrolytes repleted quickly.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.900
Otherwise they can go
into hypovolemic shock.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.800
Their kidneys can shut
down and they could die

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.740
as a result of this dehydration.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.573
(whimsical music)

00:05:52.508 --> 00:05:53.976
- Heads up!
- Huh?

00:05:53.976 --> 00:05:55.557
(can thudding)
Ah!

00:05:55.557 --> 00:05:56.390
(body thudding)

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.360
- A lot of people don't realize,

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.580
when you fall on your back,

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.920
you really don't support your head well

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.130
so your head ends up hitting afterwards.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.300
Your brain actually suffers
trauma onto the side

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.380
that you got hit

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.820
as well as the other side of the brain.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.160
It's actually called a
countercoup type of injury

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.590
where the brain slides to the back,

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:14.900
hits the back of the skull,

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.920
but then because you landed and you shake,

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.480
it actually hits the
front of the skull as well

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.339
so you have injury on
both sides of the brain.

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:22.422
- Don't move.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.214
- Marv, what are you doing?

00:06:26.214 --> 00:06:27.047
Marv.

00:06:27.047 --> 00:06:28.910
(crowbar thudding)
Ah geez!

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.230
- Oh my God.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:33.010
Not only can you fracture
ribs in the sternum,

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:37.740
if you hit like the point of
maximum impulse from the heart

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:40.020
and you hit it right at the wrong time,

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:41.260
in the middle of its beat,

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.830
you can actually stop
the heart from beating.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.170
This is like a known phenomenon
in little league baseball.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.790
If you hit a grounder
and it hits the child

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.260
in the chest right at that moment,

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.650
it could actually stop the heart.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:53.010
And that's why there's
mandated defibrillators

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.010
that need to be present
at little league games

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:57.575
because of this.

00:06:57.575 --> 00:07:01.173
(suspenseful music)

00:07:01.173 --> 00:07:03.920
(woman gasps)

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:04.753
- Well, hello.

00:07:06.154 --> 00:07:08.824
(fist thudding)
(Marv grunting)

00:07:08.824 --> 00:07:10.427
- He did it.

00:07:10.427 --> 00:07:11.529
- Did what?

00:07:11.529 --> 00:07:12.362
(fist thudding)
(Harry grunting)

00:07:12.362 --> 00:07:14.850
- She's a strong punch
for a one-punch knockout.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.810
It's easy, easy to break
a facial bone here.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.800
Easy, easy to get a concussion here.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.360
I feel like this is what Logan Paul

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.813
versus Floyd Mayweather's gonna look like.

00:07:22.813 --> 00:07:25.480
(horns blaring)

00:07:27.633 --> 00:07:29.759
(electricity buzzing)

00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:30.592
(Marv yelling)

00:07:30.592 --> 00:07:31.425
When you get electrocuted

00:07:31.425 --> 00:07:32.270
through an alternating current,

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:33.860
it's actually really difficult to let go

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.980
of whatever object is
causing electrocution

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.130
and you can start
developing muscle spasms,

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:41.920
cramps, shaking, arrhythmias
of your heart, seizures.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.460
All these things start going

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.750
because your body has a
natural electrical gradient.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.890
The way that your heart beats,

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:49.870
the way that your brain fires,

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.110
once that is interrupted

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.680
by this extraneous bit of electricity

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.129
it's incredibly painful
and damaging to your body.

00:07:57.129 --> 00:07:59.511
- I'm coming Harry!
- Marv!

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:02.594
(Harry yelling)
- No.

00:08:05.132 --> 00:08:06.449
(body thudding)
No.

00:08:06.449 --> 00:08:08.370
We actually have criteria that we follow

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:11.280
of when we should be
cat scanning folks head

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.680
when they come in from a trauma

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.570
and part of that criteria

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.440
is knowing the mechanism of injury.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:20.010
Falling 40 feet from
the air onto a metal car

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:21.580
and having it shatter like this

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.100
is the definition of needing a cat scan.

00:08:25.357 --> 00:08:29.190
(brick whirling)
(brick thudding)

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:33.240
Brick from the fourth story,
whatever that is, to the head.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.480
You're not getting up from that.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.860
If it hits on an angle
especially, that's death.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.263
First of all, good aim, but that's death.

00:08:41.471 --> 00:08:42.592
(brick whirling)

00:08:42.592 --> 00:08:43.425
(brick thudding)
(Harry yelling)

00:08:43.425 --> 00:08:44.260
Oh my God.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:47.930
The second concussion is
always worse than the first.

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.170
When you get your first concussion,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.260
your brain gets shaken up.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.950
There's inflammatory cells.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.950
Your brain is very susceptible

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.730
to getting permanently injured.

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:58.370
So, right here, the fact
that he got one concussion

00:08:58.370 --> 00:08:59.790
and then got hit with another brick,

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.640
he's getting six months of headaches,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.480
six months of light sensitivity,

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.970
if not dying immediately,

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:06.461
like I don't know what's happening.

00:09:06.461 --> 00:09:08.627
(brick whirling)
(Marv yelling)

00:09:08.627 --> 00:09:10.793
(brick thudding)
Oh my God!

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:13.905
Oh my God.

00:09:13.905 --> 00:09:15.167
(nail shooting)

00:09:15.167 --> 00:09:17.606
(Marv yelling)

00:09:17.606 --> 00:09:18.620
(nail shooting)

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.100
There's so much wrong with that.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.700
He got shot in the groin with a nail.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.360
That's gonna need a urologist.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.270
Like that's gonna need urgent surgery.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.450
You need to see if any
structures were damaged.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:29.900
You need to put it back together.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.150
In the face?

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.680
There's nerves in the face.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.670
You can disrupt nerves.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.753
You can lose sensation in the face.

00:09:35.753 --> 00:09:40.753
(whimsical music)
(Harry laughing)

00:09:41.186 --> 00:09:43.415
(hands squishing)
(harry yelling)

00:09:43.415 --> 00:09:44.248
(body thudding)

00:09:44.248 --> 00:09:45.081
Okay.

00:09:45.081 --> 00:09:46.140
Like when you hear about people

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.520
who survive skydiving accidents or falls,

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.290
it's almost usually because
something broke their fall

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.960
or they fell onto a hill where it was

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.090
like an angle and their
momentum carried them

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.980
and they didn't just
come to a complete stop.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:59.160
My man here came to a complete stop.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.260
Why is that dangerous?

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.140
'Cause your body comes to a complete stop,

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:03.590
but the force doesn't.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.940
So, the force goes right
through everything.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.420
All of the organs smash
against themselves,

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.168
the bones break 'cause they're hitting.

00:10:11.168 --> 00:10:12.001
Uh.

00:10:12.001 --> 00:10:12.930
- Harry!

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.523
I've reached the top.

